    "stem": "Sonia knows that lines $m$ and $n$ are parallel. Transversal $s$ crosses both lines. Angle $u$ measures $55^{\\circ}$. Angle $v$ is alternate to angle $u$.\n\nWhich statements are correct?",
    "item_type": "three_statement",
    "options": {
      "A": "1 only",
      "B": "1 and 2 only",
      "C": "2 and 3 only",
      "D": "1, 2 and 3"
    },
    "statements": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "text": "Angle $v$ equals $55^{\\circ}$ because alternate angles are equal when the lines are parallel."
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "text": "Angle $v$ equals $55^{\\circ}$ even if $m$ and $n$ are not parallel."
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "text": "The same alternate-angle equality holds for any two lines cut by a transversal, parallel or not."
      }
